                "known to vanish on the root graph."
            ),
        },
        "global_unit_boundary": {
            "rbar_on_Rminus": "-2*G3 on q=0",
            "gcd_q_G3": "1 (no common component)",
            "rbar_is_a_global_unit_on_the_projective_conic": False,
            "consequence": (
                "A valid global homotopy must use the denominator-free matrix "
                "factorization; it may not divide by w-G3."
            ),
        },
        "checks": {
            "the_selected_root_curve_lies_on_the_exact_K3": True,
            "the_H4_quotient_is_integral_and_coprime_to_q": True,
            "both_two_by_two_matrix_factorization_identities_replay": True,
            "all_six_selected_source_normal_pairs_replay": True,
            "the_normal_transfer_uses_no_denominator": True,
        },
        "guardrails": {
            "claims_rbar_is_globally_invertible_on_the_root_curve": False,
            "claims_the_matrix_factorization_alone_selects_the100_plane": False,
            "claims_component20_rank36_over_Qgamma": False,
            "claims_global_H02_rank_equality": False,
            "claims_a_physical_endpoint": False,
        },
        "theorem": {
            "name": "ustG3fjComponent20K3RootNormalMatrixFactorization",
            "tier": "CLOSED_EXACT_DENOMINATOR_FREE_ROOT_NORMAL_TRANSFER",
            "statement": (
                "The frozen q79 K3 equation has the exact decomposition "
                "K3=(w+G3)(w-G3)+(xz-y^2)H4 with integral quartic H4 coprime "
                "to q. The displayed matrices M and N factor K3 in both orders. "
                "The selected G3FI source pair (B6,D7) is mapped by the first row "
                "of M to A0_selected-A1 in every Q(gamma) coordinate. This closes "
                "the denominator-free two-normal transfer object, while selection "
